hadiths[43]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3652","Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said: A person in the state of Ihram cannot marry himself nor can he marry anyone."
"3653","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him), he was not in the state of Ihram at that time."
"3654","Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, he was not in Ihram, and when Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) left, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was not in Ihram."
"3655","Yazid bin Asm narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimuna, he was not in the state of Ihram, and when Sayyida Maimuna passed away, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was not in the state of Ihram."
"3656","Sayyida Maimoona bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at the place of Saraf, and we were not in the state of Ihram at that time."
"3657","Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, both of them were not in Ihram."
"3658","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maimuna (may Allah be pleased with him), he was not in the state of Ihram, and when Maimuna (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, the Prophet (may Allah's prayers and peace be upon him) was not in the state of Ihram."
"3659","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him), he was not in the state of Ihram, and when Sayyida Maimunah left, he was not in the state of Ihram either. A narrator named Dawood Abu Amr is Dawood Ibn Zubarqan."
"3660","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mahmiyah bin Jaz and two people to Sayyidah Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him) to give her the message of marriage. (uncle) entrusted to Sayyidna Abbas (RA) then Sayyidna Abbas (RA) arranged the marriage of Sayyida Maimuna with the Prophet (PBUH)."
"3661","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), he was not in the state of Ihram at that time."
"3662","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), he was not in a good condition at that time."
"3663","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), both of them were not in good health."
"3664","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), he was not in a good condition at that time."
"3665","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3666","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got married (with Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him)) he was not in a state at that time."
"3667","Narrated Urwa bin Zubair: He asked Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa about this saying of Allah: ""And if you fear that you will not be able to do justice to the orphan girls, then marry two or four of the women you like."" Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O my nephew, this refers to an orphan girl who was brought up by a person, and that girl was a sharer in his wealth. If that person was interested in the wealth and beauty of this girl, then the guardian wanted to marry her, so that she would not have to pay dowry according to justice. Marry the girls or ask the Ansar to give them Mahrad. These people were ordered to marry other women whom they did not like. Narrated ``Urwa: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: After this verse, people asked various questions about it, so Allah revealed this verse: ""People ask you about women: Say: Allah commands you about them, and about the orphan girls that have been recited in the Book, the orphan girls whom you do not pay what they have been appointed for youth and you are interested in marrying them."" What Allah has mentioned here, that the verses of the Book of Allah that have been recited before you, refers to the previous verse, in which Allah Almighty said: ""And if you fear that you will not be able to deal with the orphan girls fairly, then the women you like best."" Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: In the second verse, Allah says: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that people were forbidden to marry orphan girls whom they were attracted to by their wealth and beauty: when they paid them according to justice, this was because if such girls had little wealth or less beauty, the guardians should not be attracted to them."
"3668","Narrated ``Urwa bin Zubair: He asked Sayyida Aisha (RA) about this saying of Allah: And if you fear that you will not be able to deal with orphan girls justly, marry two or four of the women you like.'' Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) said: O my nephew, this means an orphan girl who was brought up by a person, and that girl was a sharer in his wealth. If that person was interested in the wealth and beauty of this girl, then the guardian wanted to marry her, so that she would not have to pay as dowry according to justice. So the people were forbidden to marry these girls in this way, or else to marry them justly (i.e. according to common custom) and they were ordered to marry other women. Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, said: In the second verse, Allah Ta'ala has said: ""And you do not take heart in marrying them."" That is, a person is not interested in marrying an orphan girl who is brought up under his care, whose wealth and beauty are less, so people were forbidden to marry those orphan girls whose wealth and beauty people are interested in (because otherwise) their interest ends, but if they do away with them according to justice (the ruling will be different)."
"3669","Narrated Urwa bin Zubair: He asked Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) about this saying of Allah: And if you fear that you will not be able to deal with orphan girls justly, then marry two, or three or four women whom you like. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O my nephew, this means an orphan girl who was brought up by a person, and that girl was a sharer in his wealth, and if that person was interested in the wealth and beauty of that girl, then the guardian wanted to marry her, so that she would not have to pay the dowry according to justice. Marry these girls, or rather give them Mehrad Akrin justly (i.e. according to common custom). These people were ordered to marry other women. Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha: Then the people asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Allah revealed this verse. ""People ask you about women, then say, Allah commands you about them, and about the orphan girls that have been recited in the Book, to whom you do not pay what is prescribed for a young man, and you are interested in marrying her."" Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha: In this verse, Allah Ta'ala has explained this command to the people, if someone is beautiful and rich, then people are interested in marrying her, but they do not give her full Mahrada according to the general custom, but if the girl is lacking in terms of beauty and wealth, then they do not marry her, but look for other women. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha: When these people do not feel interested in such girls and they abandon them, then they do not have the right to marry such girls when they feel attracted to them, but if they treat them fairly and pay the dowry in full (then the ruling will be different). Their subject is mutually exclusive."
"3670","Hisham bin Urwah narrates the statement of Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding his father (Urwah bin Zubair): If you fear that you will not be able to do justice to the orphan girls, then marry those women whom you like. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: It means an orphan girl who was raised by a person, that person was the guardian of that girl, and then married her because of her wealth, but he did not want to keep her with him and did not deal with her fairly even in wealth."
"3671","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Avoid marrying four types of people: madness, insanity, leprosy (leprosy) leprosy."
"3672","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: If a woman is married to a person fraudulently, and the woman has insanity, leprosy, or leprosy, the woman will receive dowry, because the man has had intercourse with her, and the man will receive the dowry from the guardian of the woman, who married her fraudulently."
"3673","Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave this ruling regarding a woman suffering from insanity, if her husband has sexual relations with her, then separation will be made between the two wives."
"3674","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It is not permissible to sell four types of women (whether they are concubines) or to marry them (if they are freedmen), a mad woman, a leprosy woman, a leprous woman, and a woman suffering from the disease of genital swelling."
"3675","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""Whoever marries a woman who is insane, leprous, fecund, fertile, or has an obstacle in her private life, then that woman is considered his wife. If a man wishes, he should let her live with him, otherwise he should divorce her."""
"3676","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Amr ibn al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Sayyidna Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) about the constant fear of harming his wife."
"3677","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No lawful thing becomes unlawful because of something forbidden."""
"3678","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who commits a forbidden act with a woman and then marries her daughter, or marries a woman's mother after committing a forbidden act with a woman."
"3679","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): No haram thing makes a haram thing haram."
"3680","Sayyida Aisha (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a person who had committed adultery with a woman and then later wanted to marry the same woman or perhaps her daughter. The Prophet (PBUH) said, ""Nothing forbidden does not make something lawful. Haram is established only when marriage has taken place first."""
"3681","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) was asked about a man who commits a forbidden act: then later they want to marry, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Their act was adultery, but the second act (will be considered marriage)."
"3682","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Allah will not have mercy on a person who looks at the private parts of a woman and her daughter. This hadith) is suspended and the narrator named Hamad bin Abu Sulaiman has been declared weak."
"3683","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama accepted Islam and had ten wives. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him: He should keep four of them with him, and separate from the rest. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: When Sayyidna Safwan Bin Umayyah accepted Islam, he had eight wives, so the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to keep four of them with him and to separate from the rest."
"3684","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama (RA) accepted Islam. He had ten wives. The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to marry four of them."
"3685","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salamah accepted Islam, he had ten wives during the time of Jahiliyyah. These women also accepted Islam with him. The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to adopt four of them. A narrator named Ramadi narrates: The people of Basra narrated in the same way."
"3686","Uthman bin Abu Sawid narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this to Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama, when he accepted Islam and he had ten wives at that time, (the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said) Keep four of them with you and separate from the rest."
"3687","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3688","Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this to a man belonging to the Thaqeef tribe (following this is according to the previous hadith)."
"3689","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3690","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: When he accepted Islam, he had eight wives, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take four of them."
"3691","Qays bin Harith Kalbi, about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrates the Hadith: A man belonging to Banwasad accepted Islam, he had eight wives, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, take four of them, so he said: O so-and-so woman, you come, O so-and-so woman, you come, O so-and-so woman, you go, O so-and-so woman, you go."
"3692","A narrator named Mugheera narrates on the authority of one of the descendants of Sayyidna Harith bin Qays Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him: When Sayyidna Harith bin Qays Asdi, may Allah be pleased with him, accepted Islam, he had eight wives, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him to marry four of them."
"3693","A narrator named Mugheera narrates on the authority of Rabi bin Qays: When his great-grandfather Sayyiduna Harith bin Qays Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him, accepted Islam, he had eight wives, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him to marry four of them."
"3694","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama Al-Thaqafi accepted Islam, he had ten wives at that time, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to keep four of them with him. During the time of Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salamah divorced these women, so Sayyidna Umar, Radi Allahu Anhu instructed them to approach these women. There are these words in a hadith: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to them: You should approach them, otherwise I will make them the heirs of your property, and I will give an order about your grave. There are these words in a hadith: When they accepted Islam, these women also accepted Islam along with them."
